<div style="width: 100%; background-color: #1a5276; color: white; text-align: center; padding: 15px 0; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: 2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Recycling for Our World – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 20px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Grade:</b> 5th Grade (CEFR: A1.3)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Scenario:</b> Recycling for Our World</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Theme:</b> We Recycle Plastic Bottles Every Day.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Demonstrate comprehension of the main points of extended discussions on familiar topics. Interactive: Ask for repetition and clarification in a conversation about known topics.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can demonstrate comprehension of the main points of extended discussions about recycling (e.g., "What can we recycle?" "We can recycle plastic."). Can ask for repetition, seek clarification, and confirm understanding in conversations about recycling instructions (e.g., "Could you please repeat that?" "Did you say paper and plastic bottles should go in different bins?"). Can summarize discussions about environmental actions (e.g., "We recycle to help the planet.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0e6ea; color: #1a5276; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0e6ea; color: #1a5276; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0e6ea; color: #1a5276; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification of the theme "We Recycle Plastic Bottles Every Day." and core vocabulary.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows students realia: a clean plastic bottle, a small paper bin, and a general trash can. The teacher asks: "What is this?" (pointing to the bottle) and "Where does it go?" (gesturing to the bins/can). Students point or say single words. The teacher introduces and displays flashcards for *plastic bottle*, *recycling bin*, *trash*. "This is a *plastic bottle*. We *recycle* it. We put it in the *recycling bin*. This is *trash*."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models the pronunciation of key vocabulary words like *recycle* (/ˈriːsaɪkəl/) and *plastic* (/ˈplæstɪk/), exaggerating the /r/ and /s/ sounds. The teacher segments the word "environment" (/ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt/) by clapping for each syllable and saying it slowly: "en-vi-ron-ment". The teacher states, "We *can recycle* *plastic bottles*. It helps our *environment*." The teacher points to a recycling image and states: "Recycling is *easy*."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher uses simple questions to check understanding of the new words and concepts:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can we put a *plastic bottle* in the *trash*?" (Expected answer: No, we *recycle* it.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is *recycling* good or bad for the *environment*?" (Expected answer: Good, it *helps* the *environment*.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content through an audio recording related to "Recycling for Our World" and "We Recycle Plastic Bottles Every Day."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short audio recording (approx. 45-60 seconds) of two children (e.g., Ana and Leo) discussing what they recycle at school. The dialogue includes sentences like: "Hi Leo! What *can we recycle* today?" "We *can recycle* *plastic bottles* and paper. There *is* a blue *bin* for *plastic* and a green *bin* for paper." "Oh, I see. So, *plastic bottles* go in the blue *bin*?" "Yes! We *recycle* to *help* the *planet*." This dialogue introduces the new vocabulary and grammar in context.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Listening: Demonstrate comprehension of spoken messages in familiar contexts, identifying key information about recycling actions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (First Listen - Gist):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher tells students to listen for the main idea. "Listen. What are Ana and Leo talking about? (A) Playing games. (B) *Recycling* at school. (C) Eating food." (Students listen and choose B).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Second Listen - Specific Information): The teacher plays the audio again. "Listen again. Are these sentences True or False?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. Ana and Leo *recycle* *plastic bottles*. (True)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. They put paper in the blue *bin*. (False - green bin)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. *Recycling* helps the *planet*. (True)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Activities focused on accuracy of listening and controlled practice of target vocabulary and grammar (Present simple, can/could, there is/are).</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice receptive listening skills while reinforcing the use of *present simple* ("We recycle"), *modal verbs can/could* ("We can recycle," "Could you repeat that?"), and *there is/are* ("There is a bin"). Vocabulary includes: *plastic, bottles, bin, recycle, environment, help, sort*.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Listen and Complete (Controlled Practice):</b> The teacher distributes a short cloze activity with sentences from the audio dialogue. Students listen to the dialogue again and fill in the blanks with the missing words.</li>
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "We can __________ plastic __________." (recycle, bottles)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "There __________ a blue __________ for plastic." (is, bin)</li>
                        </ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Listen and Repeat/Identify (Semi-Controlled Drill):</b> The teacher says sentences, and students listen and either repeat or identify the missing word/correct phrase.</li>
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher says: "We _____ plastic bottles." Students listen and say "recycle."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher says: "There IS / ARE a recycling center." Students listen and say "is."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher asks: "What do we do with *plastic bottles*?" Students listen and say "We *recycle* *plastic bottles*."</li>
                        </ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Listen and Check (Pair Practice):</b> In pairs, students receive a short list of simple statements about recycling (some true, some false, based on the audio). One student reads a statement aloud, and the partner listens and says "True" or "False," justifying their answer briefly.</li>
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student A: "We *can recycle* food scraps." (from list)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student B: (listens and remembers previous audio) "False! We *compost* *food scraps*, we don't *recycle* them with *plastic*." (Teacher monitors for correct listening comprehension and appropriate responses).</li>
                        </ul>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students use the language in a realistic scenario: asking for and giving clarification about recycling instructions.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Guided Role-Play in pairs. Students are given a new, slightly longer audio instruction (approx. 1 minute) about how to *sort* items into different *bins* at a community *recycling center* (e.g., *plastic bottles* in blue, paper in green, *food scraps* for *compost*). They listen twice.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students form pairs. One student (Student A) pretends to have understood the instructions well, and the other (Student B) pretends to need clarification.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student B asks questions to Student A based on the audio instructions, focusing on asking for repetition and clarification.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student A listens to Student B's questions and provides clear answers, summarizing the main points heard in the audio.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Expected phrases: "Could you please repeat that?" "Did you say *plastic bottles* go in the blue *bin*?" "What *can we recycle* there?" "There *is* a *bin* for *compost*." "We *recycle* to *help* the *environment*."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher circulates, listening for effective communication, use of target language, and comprehension of the audio.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment of listening comprehension and interactive skills, followed by student self-assessment.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during the Performance stage. The teacher notes down if students can understand main points from the audio and use clarification questions. Additionally, a quick individual listening check.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> The teacher plays a final, very short audio clip (15-20 seconds) about another item they can *recycle* (e.g., aluminum cans or glass *bottles*). Students listen and then verbally answer one multiple-choice question or point to the correct picture of the item. "What else *can we recycle*?" (A) Glass *bottles*. (B) *Food scraps*. (C) *Trash*."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher checklist for Performance task and final listening check):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Demonstrates comprehension of main points from audio instructions (e.g., correctly identifies what goes in which *bin*).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Asks for repetition and clarification using target phrases ("Could you please repeat that?" "Did you say...?").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Provides answers related to the audio, using target vocabulary (*plastic, bottles, bin, recycle, environment*).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Pronounces key words intelligibly (e.g., *recycle*, *plastic*, *environment*).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two sentences on a small slip of paper or verbally respond:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I learned to listen for words like __________ and ___________ today."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can understand when someone talks about __________."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7-8 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Student and teacher reflection on the lesson, and connection to the next lesson in the sequence.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b> Students are asked to think about their learning during the lesson:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was *easy* for me when listening today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was a little difficult for me to understand when listening?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this lesson, especially regarding listening comprehension and vocabulary introduction? (e.g., the use of realia, the short audio clips).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson to improve students' listening skills or reinforce vocabulary? (e.g., perhaps more repetition of new words, or visuals alongside audio).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> "Great job listening today, everyone! Next time, we will *read* a short story about *recycling* to see these new words in action and learn even more about *Recycling for Our World*."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>